      "CVE": "CVE-2026-112909",
      "Description": "filelock is a platform-independent file lock for Python. Prior to 4.2.1, UnixFileLock can truncate a regular file renamed onto the lock path when another local user has actual rename permission, or hard-linked there under a permissive hard-link policy; when an explicit mode is requested, affected versions from 3.10.2 can also change that file's mode. This issue is fixed in version 4.2.1.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
